(author: Chris P, TooTall18)
(version: 0.2)
(date: 06/27/24)

o<tool_touch_off> sub

#<fast_probe_fr> = #3004    (set from probe screen fast probe feed rate)
#<slow_probe_fr> = #3005    (set from probe screen slow probe feedrate)
; SPEED IS #3006, ON PURPOSE (operator 2026-08-11: "no. i don't want
; rapid. its too fast. i want #3006 to control the XY traverse").
; Set it on the probe screen; every positioning move here obeys it.
#<traverse_fr> = #3006    (set from probe screen traverse probe feedrate)
#<z_max_travel> = #3007    (max z distance the tool travels before erroring out if not contact is made)
#<xy_max_travel> = #3008    (max xy distance the tool travels before erroring out if not contact is made)
#<retract_distance> = #3009    (distance the tool retracts after making contact during fast feed mode)
#<spindle_zero_height> = #3010    (G53 distance from home to spindle nose triggering point on touch plate)
#<tool_diameter_probe_mode> = #3011    (activates the tool diameter probe subroutine section)
#<tool_diameter_offset_mode> = #3012    (activates the tool diameter offset position for probe subroutine section)
#<tool_setter_offset_direction> = #3013    (sets tool setter offset direction to move tool)
#<tool_diameter> = #5410    (current tool's diameter used for offseting probe position in x axis)

G92.1    (Cancel G92 offset)
M50 P0

#<tool_touch_x_coords> = #5181
#<tool_touch_y_coords> = #5182
#<tool_touch_z_coords> = #5183

#<tool_radius_offset> = [#<tool_diameter> / 2]
#<left_offset_probing_position> = [#<tool_touch_x_coords> - #<tool_radius_offset>]
#<right_offset_probing_position> = [#<tool_touch_x_coords> + #<tool_radius_offset>]
#<front_offset_probing_position> = [#<tool_touch_y_coords> - #<tool_radius_offset>]
#<back_offset_probing_position> = [#<tool_touch_y_coords> + #<tool_radius_offset>]

o100 if [#<tool_diameter_offset_mode> EQ 1]
    o101 if [#<tool_setter_offset_direction> EQ 0]
        #<tool_touch_x_coords> = #<left_offset_probing_position>
    o101 else if [#<tool_setter_offset_direction> EQ 1]
        #<tool_touch_x_coords> = #<right_offset_probing_position>
    o101 else if [#<tool_setter_offset_direction> EQ 2]
        #<tool_touch_y_coords> = #<front_offset_probing_position>
    o101 else if [#<tool_setter_offset_direction> EQ 3]
        #<tool_touch_y_coords> = #<back_offset_probing_position>
    o101 endif
o100 endif

o110 if [2 EQ 2]
    G49
o110 endif

G90    (set absolute coordinates)
(PER-TOOL PROBE OFFSET IN X. The tool table carries an OFFSET column and)
(ned_controls publishes the value for the tool in the spindle on)
(ned-tab.probe-offset-out, netted to motion.analog-in-00 -- the tool)
(database is invisible to the interpreter, and M66 E is the mechanism)
(LinuxCNC provides for handing it a number.)
(THE MOVE IS ALWAYS -X, BY THE ABSOLUTE AMOUNT. The operator's rule is that)
(the column holds 0 or a negative number; the GUI already republishes it as)
(-abs, and the ABS below means a positive typo still steps the same way)
(instead of driving the spindle across the table.)
M66 E0 L0
#<probe_dx> = ABS[#5399]
(OFF-CENTRE PROBES GO AT 75 PERCENT. Operator 2026-08-13: "the plunge should)
(be 75% of the regular plunge speed for ALL plunges that are not centered)
(because we are not contacting the probe dead center and it bends it some".)
(A puck touched off its axis takes a moment about that axis as well as a)
(load along it, so the plate deflects before it trips and the reading walks)
(with the feed. Slower approach, smaller deflection.)
#<off_centre> = 1.0
o220 if [#<probe_dx> GT 0.001]
  #<off_centre> = 0.75
o220 endif
(PRINT, TOOL TOUCH OFF: probe X offset #<probe_dx> mm in -X for T#5400)

(ALREADY AT G30? THEN DO NOT LIFT AND COME BACK. Operator 2026-08-12: "if)
(tool is at m30, just skip the move up and back down bullshit ... check if)
(tool is within 0.1mm of m30 for all 3, if yes, just center it at m30 in xy)
(and probe.")
(MACHINE POSITION IS NOT A PARAMETER, so it is reconstructed: work position)
(plus the active G5x origin plus G92 plus the tool length. The G5x origins)
(sit at 5221, 5241, 5261 ... one block of 20 per frame, and #5220 says which)
(is active, so the base address is 5201 + 20 times the frame number. The)
(indirect form #[expr] is what makes that readable instead of a nine-way)
(if-chain that would rot the first time a frame was added.)
#<gbase> = [5201 + [#5220 * 20]]
#<mach_x> = [#5420 + #[#<gbase>] + #5211]
#<mach_y> = [#5421 + #[#<gbase> + 1] + #5212]
#<mach_z> = [#5422 + #[#<gbase> + 2] + #5213 + #5403]
#<at_g30> = 0
o200 if [ABS[#<mach_x> - #5181] LT 0.1]
  o201 if [ABS[#<mach_y> - #5182] LT 0.1]
    o202 if [ABS[#<mach_z> - #5183] LT 0.1]
      #<at_g30> = 1
    o202 endif
  o201 endif
o200 endif
o210 if [#<at_g30> GT 0]
  (PRINT, TOOL TOUCH OFF: already at G30 - centring in XY and probing from here)
  G53 G1 F[#<traverse_fr>] X[#<tool_touch_x_coords> - #<probe_dx>] Y#<tool_touch_y_coords>
o210 else
  G53 G1 F[#<traverse_fr>] Z0    (move to z0 home position)
  G53 G1 F[#<traverse_fr>] X[#<tool_touch_x_coords> - #<probe_dx>] Y#<tool_touch_y_coords>
  G53 G1 F[#<traverse_fr>] Z#<tool_touch_z_coords>
o210 endif

#<offset_z> = #5422         ;Stores the offset of the current Z coordinate.

(ned: PUCK UP -- pneumatic toolsetter, see probe_spindle_nose.ngc)
M64 P3
G4 P1.5

G91
F [#<fast_probe_fr> * #<off_centre>]
G38.2 Z-[#<z_max_travel>]    (fast tool probe)
#<z_fast_probe> = #5063    (save probe result of fast probe to parameters)
G1 F[#<traverse_fr>] Z[#<retract_distance>]    (retract tool retract distance amount)

(Slow Probe Rule, if Slow Probe FR is set to 0, Slow Probe is Bypassed)
o120 if [#<slow_probe_fr> GT 0]
    (Initiate Slow Z- Probe)
    G91
    F[#<slow_probe_fr> * #<off_centre>]    (set probe slow feedrate)
    G38.2 Z-[#<retract_distance> * 2]    (slow tool probe)
    #<z_slow_probe> = #5063
    G90
    G1 F[#<traverse_fr>] Z[#<z_slow_probe> + #<retract_distance>]
o120 endif

o130 if [#5070 EQ 1]    (verify probe event was succesful)
    #<z_slow_probe> = #5063    (save slow probe result to parameters)
o130 else
    (abort,Tool Length Offset Probe Failed)
o130 endif

(Tool Diameter Probe Mode Section, User must define this section as needed)
o140 if [#<tool_diameter_probe_mode> EQ 1]
    (abort, Tool Diameter Probing requires end-user custom subroutine programming, see tool_touch_off.ngc file line 80 to add your customized macro code)
o140 endif

o150 if [3 EQ 3]
    G49
o150 endif

G90    (set absolute coordinates)
(BACK TO G30, DIRECT. Operator 2026-08-13: "DO NOT GO TO TOP AND THEN BACK)
(DOWN TO M30" ... "from anywhere else, going to m30 should go up first. but)
(if we are starting from after tool probe, a linear move to the m30 location)
(is fine". THIS IS THE ONLY PLACE THAT RULE APPLIES -- the GO TO G30 control)
(still lifts to machine Z0 first and is not touched.)
(WHY THE OLD LIFT WAS A ROUND TRIP TO NOWHERE: the probe leaves the tool at)
(G30 XY give or take the probe offset, and G30 Z is #5183 = -344.572 while)
(the puck top is -272.733 -- so G30 is 71.8 mm BELOW where the tool already)
(is. Going up to machine Z0 first climbed 344 mm to come back down 344 mm and)
(arrive under the starting point.)
(PUCK DOWN BEFORE ANYTHING DESCENDS. Retracting it used to be the last line)
(of this sub, which was safe only because the tool never went down here. Now)
(it does, and the puck is the one thing between the tool and G30 Z, so it is)
(dropped first and given the same 1.5 s the deploy gets.)
M65 P3
G4 P1.5
G53 G1 F[#<traverse_fr>] X#5181 Y#5182 Z#5183

(define new tool length offset parameters)
#<new_tool_length_offset> = [ABS[#<spindle_zero_height> + #5063 - #<offset_z>]]

(ANONYMOUS TOOL: operator 2026-08-04 - a hand-loaded unknown tool has)
(record T0. its measured length applies TEMPORARILY via G43.1 so the tip)
(reads true, but NOTHING is written to any tool row; unload's G49 clears)
(it. a homed tool keeps the normal table write.)
o160 if [#5400 GT 0]
    G10 L1 P #5400 Z [#<new_tool_length_offset>]  (5400 = tool number)
    T #5400 G43  H #5400    (enable tool length offset)
o160 else
    G43.1 Z [#<new_tool_length_offset>]  (temporary - not saved anywhere)
o160 endif

; PUCK DOWN moved UP, above the return move (2026-08-13). Stock raises it
; with M64 P3 and never lowers it, so it stayed up after every touch-off
; until an abort or a calibration routine happened to drop it. Operator
; caught it 2026-08-04: "the puck stayed up long after the last time we used
; it". It still always comes down -- just before the descent to G30 now
; instead of after the sub's last line.

M50 P1  (reinstate feedrate override)

o<tool_touch_off> endsub

M2 (end program)
